  "title": "Truth and if",
  "blocks": [
    {
      "type": "explain",
      "md": "## Some values act as “no”\n\nIn an `if`, these are falsy: `0`, `\"\"`, `null`, `undefined`, `NaN`, `false`.\n\n`[]` and `\"0\"` are truthy. An empty list is still a list. The string zero is still text."
    },
    {
      "type": "predict",
      "id": "empty-array",
      "promptMd": "`if ([]) { \"go\" } else { \"stop\" }` yields…",
      "kind": "mcq",
      "choices": [
        {
          "id": "stop",
          "md": "`stop` — empty means false"
        },
        {
          "id": "go",
          "md": "`go` — an array object is truthy"
        }
      ],
      "answer": "go"
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "id": "label-truth",
      "engine": "javascript",
      "entry": "main.js",
      "promptMd": "> `gate(value)` returns `\"open\"` if the value is truthy, otherwise `\"shut\"`. Print `gate(0)`.",
